     "type": "text",
     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With mfa_admin deployed, both auth_dc and auth_adfs are blocked because each requires NOT mfa_admin. These are the only techniques that give foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. Without those footholds, escalate_dc and escalate_adfs cannot fire, so admin_dc and admin_adfs stay false. That means dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs, the only sources of stolen_dbadmin, are also unreachable. Every route to the data stores needs stolen_dbadmin: auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup all require it. So no foothold on db, fileserver or backup is possible, and no admin on them either. All three exfiltrate techniques require admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup, so exfiltrated cannot become true. The attacker can still get from the perimeter to reach_internal, steal user and admin credentials, and gain admin on appserver or apiserver, but cannot reach exfiltration.\"}\n```"
    }
   ],
